A qualified continuee must notify the employer in writing about the following events:  
(a) the legal divorce or legal separation from the spouse;  
(b) the loss of dependent eligibility for an insured dependent child;  
(c) a second event that would qualify the person for continuation coverage after becoming entitled to Medicare.

The 60-day notice deadline for a qualifying event starts from the latest of the following dates:
- The date the qualifying event occurs;
- The date the qualified continuee is informed of their rights under the plan;
- The date the qualified continuee is required to notify the employer or plan administrator of the qualifying event.
